  "parts": {
    "SPR-0001": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0001",
      "leaf": "This is the Big Box paper for datbox-core: laws, checklist, health, and how real a distro can get without lying about multi-user cloud.",
      "section_id": "sec-0001",
      "created_at": 1
    },
    "SPR-0002": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0002",
      "leaf": "Audience: Hands + agents building loreBOX, shotBOX, memBOX, promptBOX. Not a runnable ROM. Core is import-only.",
      "section_id": "sec-0001",
      "created_at": 2
    },
    "SPR-0003": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0003",
      "leaf": "Companion source: datbox-studio/datbox-core/README.md · freeze history: datbox-studio/docs/freeze-shot-core-lore.md",
      "section_id": "sec-0001",
      "created_at": 3
    },
    "SPR-0004": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0004",
      "leaf": "ISLANDS: each ROM = own process, own port, own safe_box, own box_sets, own card field schema. No shared mega-vault across mats.",
      "section_id": "sec-0002",
      "created_at": 4
    },
    "SPR-0005": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0005",
      "leaf": "DELIBERATE NOS: no auto-migrate myPI · no reverse-link OS in core · no multi-user/cloud yet · no character-sheet builders in DATBOX core (other product line).",
      "section_id": "sec-0002",
      "created_at": 5
    },
    "SPR-0006": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0006",
      "leaf": "YES LATER (not core now): optional card catalog product for choosing stores · catalog references only for cross-pointing · rebuild import-station/myPI from scratch when ready.",
      "section_id": "sec-0002",
      "created_at": 6
    },
    "SPR-0007": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0007",
      "leaf": "ShotBOX remains frozen until lore + core laws are happy. Do not dual-patch features across ROMs before core owns them.",
      "section_id": "sec-0002",
      "created_at": 7
    },
    "SPR-0008": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0008",
      "leaf": "CLARIFICATION (Hands): “same settings” means the SAME SCHEMA and UX grammar — NOT one settings file forced onto every DATBOX on the machine, and NOT across product lines (BBC, Charlie’s, DATBOX).",
      "section_id": "sec-0003",
      "created_at": 8
    },
    "SPR-0009": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0009",
      "leaf": "Each ROM holds: prod/box_sets/desk_prefs.json\nKeys (v1): version, theme (light|dark|system), safe_compact (bool), window_mode (compact|standard|expanded|maximized).\nloreBOX can be Compact window while shotBOX is Expanded. Independent islands, identical knobs.",
      "section_id": "sec-0003",
      "created_at": 9,
      "as_pre": true
    },
    "SPR-0010": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0010",
      "leaf": "Window mode is restored by the ROM launcher reading desk_prefs and passing --window-mode to Deck Host (cold start). In-session changes write the same file. Geometry tables live in Deck Host profiles; core only names the mode keys.",
      "section_id": "sec-0003",
      "created_at": 10
    },
    "SPR-0011": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0011",
      "leaf": "Never put desk_prefs in a shared AppData bucket for “all DATBOX.” User data may later sit beside the install, but still per-ROM paths: …/loreBOX/data/desk_prefs.json vs …/shotBOX/data/…",
      "section_id": "sec-0003",
      "created_at": 11
    },
    "SPR-0012": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0012",
      "leaf": "NEW ROM CHECKLIST\n\n[ ] Island folder: datbox-studio/{name}-box/\n[ ] MatProfile: rom_slug, bag_ext, legacy_ext, mat, house\n[ ] Port unique (not 42929 lore, not 43001 shot)\n[ ] prod/safe_box/ + _{rom_slug}.datshelf via SafeVault\n[ ] prod/box_sets/desk_prefs.json + relation_types if needed\n[ ] server.py: core on sys.path, /datbox-core/* static, /api/prefs, /api/health\n[ ] run-in-deck-host.py: profile desk (default), --window-mode from desk_prefs\n[ ] DECK_ROM_MENU: New Viewer · Reload ROM · Settings · About · Exit\n[ ] DatboxDesk dialogs only (no window.confirm)\n[ ] Card fields ROM-specific; Machina peek/stamp optional same protocol\n[ ] README + optional company lorebox card",
      "section_id": "sec-0004",
      "created_at": 12,
      "as_pre": true
    },
    "SPR-0013": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0013",
      "leaf": "HEALTH PAYLOAD (minimum):\n{ \"ok\": true, \"app\": \"loreBOX\", \"house\": \"DATBOX\", \"core\": \"datbox-core\", \"shelf\": \"_lorebox.datshelf\", \"port\": 42929 }",
      "section_id": "sec-0004",
      "created_at": 13,
      "as_pre": true
    },
    "SPR-0014": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0014",
      "leaf": "CSS expectation: one data-driven chrome. Per-ROM difference is primarily palette/theme tokens, not a second layout language. Core may hold desk_dialog + future density tokens; ROM app.css is palette + local density until lifted.",
      "section_id": "sec-0004",
      "created_at": 14
    },
    "SPR-0015": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0015",
      "leaf": "Static core mount: GET /datbox-core/* → datbox-studio/datbox-core/{js,css}/… (no .. escape). Future: shared Python helper so every server.py does not copy-paste.",
      "section_id": "sec-0004",
      "created_at": 15
    },
    "SPR-0016": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0016",
      "leaf": "STUCK SERVER PROTOCOL\n1) curl or browser: http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/health\n2) ok:true → ROM alive; if UI wrong, hard Reload ROM (cache bust), not another server.\n3) connection refused → no process; start run-*.bat again.\n4) hangs / old code → zombie on the port: find PID listening on PORT, kill only that process, restart launcher.\n5) Do not start a second server on the same port “to fix it.”",
      "section_id": "sec-0005",
      "created_at": 16,
      "as_pre": true
    },
    "SPR-0017": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0017",
      "leaf": "Windows (PowerShell) examples:\nGet-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 42929 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n# Note OwningProcess, then:\nStop-Process -Id {PID} -Force\n\nOr: netstat -ano | findstr :42929",
      "section_id": "sec-0005",
      "created_at": 17,
      "as_pre": true
    },
    "SPR-0018": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0018",
      "leaf": "Launcher should wait on HEALTH URL before opening the window (Deck Host --health). If health times out, fail loud — do not open a blank WebView and guess.",
      "section_id": "sec-0005",
      "created_at": 18
    },
    "SPR-0019": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0019",
      "leaf": "Distro future: a small “ROM doctor” action (Settings or About) that hits /api/health and shows port + shelf path + prefs path. Not implemented yet; protocol is frozen so it can be.",
      "section_id": "sec-0005",
      "created_at": 19
    },
    "SPR-0020": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0020",
      "leaf": "HOW REAL CAN REAL BECOME\nShip shape: one folder or installer per ROM product.\n  YourROM/\n    YourROM.exe          # Deck Host runtime configured for this ROM\n    rom/ or box_sys/     # UI + server\n    data/ or safe_box/   # user bags + desk_prefs (must survive updates)\n    datbox-core/         # vendored or next to rom (import + /datbox-core static)",
      "section_id": "sec-0006",
      "created_at": 20,
      "as_pre": true
    },
    "SPR-0021": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0021",
      "leaf": "UPDATE MODEL (honest v1):\n- No silent cloud auto-update required for first distro.\n- User installs new build; program files overwrite; USER DATA directory is never overwritten by the installer.\n- In-app “Check for updates” can later open a URL or download a package — still replace program, keep data.\n- Do not invent “patch the running Python in place” as the primary story.",
      "section_id": "sec-0006",
      "created_at": 21,
      "as_pre": true
    },
    "SPR-0022": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0022",
      "leaf": "Split install vs data NOW in design even if dev still uses prod/safe_box next to code:\n- Dev: ALICE_BOX/datbox-studio/lore-box/prod/safe_box (fine)\n- Distro: %LocalAppData%/DatBoxStudio/loreBOX/safe_box + desk_prefs (example)\nMigrating path is a launcher flag later; law is “data survives program replace.”",
      "section_id": "sec-0006",
      "created_at": 22
    },
    "SPR-0023": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0023",
      "leaf": "In-app update (future, optional): Settings → “Get update…” opens release notes URL; or downloads zip to a staging folder and prompts “Quit and install.” Core does not ship an updater binary in v1.",
      "section_id": "sec-0006",
      "created_at": 23
    },
    "SPR-0024": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0024",
      "leaf": "Shelf file upgrades: if .datshelf version bumps, SafeVault.reconcile_shelf migrates shape. Bag schema version stays on each .lorebox mat file. Never delete user bags on upgrade.",
      "section_id": "sec-0006",
      "created_at": 24
    },
    "SPR-0025": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0025",
      "leaf": "CSS: Hands notes product is data-driven; little lore-specific art. Per-ROM CSS difference is mainly palette. Split when polishing: (1) chrome/rail/dialog density (2) card editor surfaces. Core already owns desk_dialog.css; lift density tokens after Hands polish if shared.",
      "section_id": "sec-0007",
      "created_at": 25
    },
    "SPR-0026": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0026",
      "leaf": "MACHINA: current listen (peek cord/now, stamp chip on mint, hide empty TPS/VEN) is enough for core law. Future: Machina-side mute for VEN when a message references a person unrelated to the mat — product toggle on Charlie’s Toys, not a DATBOX vault feature.",
      "section_id": "sec-0007",
      "created_at": 26
    },
    "SPR-0027": {
      "part_code": "SPR-0027",
      "leaf": "Core surface freeze (importable): stem · bag IO · MatProfile · shelf · SafeVault · desk_dialog JS/CSS · (soon) static mount helper + prefs key names. Not importable: card forms, ports, company brand story, Deck Host geometry tables.",
      "section_id": "sec-0007",
      "created_at": 27
    }
  },
  "tps_chips": [],
  "updated_at": 1785100000.0
}
